quran[9]{c,v,t}:
  25,3,"Yet they have taken gods besides Him, who do not create anything and have themselves been created, and who have no control over their own harm or benefit, and have no control over (their own) death, life or resurrection."
  25,4,"The disbelievers say: ‘This is nothing but a lie which he has fabricated, and other people have helped him in (forging) it.’ So they have indeed come out with wrongdoing and falsehood."
  25,5,"And they say: ‘(This Qur’an comprises) the fables of the ancients, and they are dictated to him morning and evening.’"
  25,6,"Say: ‘He Who knows every secret in the heavens and the earth has sent it down. Surely, He is the Most Forgiving, All-Merciful.’"
  25,7,And they say: ‘What is the matter with this Messenger that he eats food and goes around in the markets? Why has an angel not been sent down to him to be a warner along with him?
  25,8,"Or (why is not) a treasure thrown to him, or (why does) he (not) have a garden from which he may eat?’ And the wrongdoers say: ‘You are just following a bewitched man (who is deprived of reason).’"
  25,9,"Look how they draw comparisons for you, so they go astray and cannot find the (right) way!"
  25,10,"Blessed is He Who will grant you better than that if He pleases—gardens with rivers flowing beneath them. Moreover, He will give you palaces."
  25,11,"Instead, they reject the Hour, and We have prepared a blazing Fire for the deniers of the Hour."
